.\" wgx.1 — manual for the wgxplore console. mdoc, OpenBSD section order.
.\" Keep in lockstep with the --help banner and the verbs in main.go.
.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt WGX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wgx ,
.Nm wgx-tui
.Nd the WireGuard networks console: declare, apply, reconcile
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm tui | Cm estate | Cm show
.Nm
.Cm net create Ar name
.Op Fl -subnet Ar CIDR
.Op Fl -topology Cm mesh | Cm hub-spoke
.Op Fl -port Ar n
.Nm
.Cm net add Ar name Ar member
.Op Fl -endpoint Ar host : Ns Ar port
.Op Fl -hub
.Nm
.Cm net render Ar name
.Nm
.Cm net up Ar name Ar member
.Nm
.Cm attach Ar net Ar container Ar member
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a keyboard-driven console for kernel WireGuard.
A network is
.Em declared
in one JSON file, rendered to plain WireGuard configuration, applied with
plain
.Xr wg 8
and
.Xr ip 8 ,
and then read back from the kernel and diffed against the declaration.
There is no daemon, no server and no agent: what
.Nm
leaves behind is stock WireGuard.
.Pp
Run with no arguments,
.Nm
opens the native GUI, falling back to the terminal console when no display
is available.
.Nm wgx-tui
is the fully static terminal-only build.
.Ss Views
.Bl -tag -width "estate"
.It Cm tui
Force the terminal console.
Estate tree on the left, dossier on the right.
.It Cm estate
Print the whole estate as a text tree, for scripts, cron and remote checks.
.It Cm show
One-shot peer dossiers for the local host.
.El
.Ss Verbs
Every mutating verb prints the literal
.Xr wg 8 Ns / Ns Xr ip 8
command before running it.
.Bl -tag -width "net render"
.It Cm net create
Declare a network.
Writes
.Pa /etc/wgx/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .json .
.It Cm net add
Add a member, generating its keypair and assigning the next address in the
subnet.
.Fl -hub
marks the reachable rendezvous of a hub-spoke network.
.It Cm net render
Compile the declaration into one configuration file per member under
.Pa /etc/wgx/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa / .
Topology is nothing but the peer list: in a mesh every member peers with
every other; in hub-spoke a spoke peers only with the hub, which carries the
whole subnet.
The kernel enforces the result through cryptokey routing.
.It Cm net up
Bring this host up as
.Ar member :
create the interface, apply the configuration, address it, and set it up.
Requires root.
.It Cm attach
Move a WireGuard interface into a running container's network namespace.
The encrypted socket stays anchored in the namespace where the interface was
created, so the tunnel keeps working while the interface lives inside the
container.
With
.Ic --network none
the mesh becomes the container's only network.
Requires root.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--topology"
.It Fl -subnet Ar CIDR
Address range for the network.
Default
.Ar 10.44.0.0/24 .
.It Fl -topology Cm mesh | Cm hub-spoke
Peer-list policy.
Default
.Cm mesh .
.It Fl -port Ar n
Listen port for members that listen.
Default
.Ar 51820 .
.It Fl -endpoint Ar host : Ns Ar port
Where other members dial this one.
Members without an endpoint roam.
.It Fl -hub
This member is the rendezvous; spokes peer only with it.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "WGXPLORE_REF" -compact
.It Ev WGXPLORE_REF
Used by downstream builds to pin the ingested revision; not read at runtime.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.config/wgx/hosts" -compact
.It Pa /etc/wgx/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .json
The declaration for one network.
The file is the API.
.It Pa /etc/wgx/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /
Rendered per-member configuration, mode 0700.
.It Pa ~/.config/wgx/hosts
Explicit estate inventory, one ssh target per line.
Takes precedence over the ssh configuration.
.It Pa /etc/wgx/hosts
System-wide inventory, same format.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
Fallback inventory.
Git forges and
.Ic gh-*
aliases are skipped.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A non-zero status accompanies a human-readable message on standard error, so
the verbs compose with
.Ic &&
and
.Ic || .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Declare a hub-spoke lab and bring the hub up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wgx net create lab --subnet 10.99.0.0/24 --topology hub-spoke
wgx net add lab hub --hub --endpoint hub.example.net:51820
wgx net add lab ct1
wgx net render lab
wgx net up lab hub
.Ed
.Pp
Give a running container exactly one network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
podman run -d --network none --name job image
wgx attach lab job ct1
.Ed
.Pp
Watch for a peer nobody declared:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wgx estate | grep -q UNDECLARED && notify "rogue WireGuard peer"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zxplore 1 ,
.Xr ip 8 ,
.Xr ip-netns 8 ,
.Xr wg 8 ,
.Xr wg-quick 8
.Sh STANDARDS
Rendered configuration is
.Xr wg 8
.Cm setconf
format and carries no
.Ic Address=
line;
.Nm
applies addresses with
.Xr ip 8 ,
which is what lets one file work before and after a namespace move.
Any WireGuard implementation can consume it.
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 2026 as the sister console to
.Xr zxplore 1 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Anthony Aq admin@zxplore.dev
.Sh CAVEATS
Reading WireGuard state requires
.Dv CAP_NET_ADMIN .
.Nm
escalates the read as gently as it can: directly when root, then
.Xr sudo 8
.Fl n ,
then
.Xr pkexec 1 .
.Pp
Member private keys currently live in the declaration file; treat
.Pa /etc/wgx
as a keystore until per-member key custody lands.
.Pp
Networks brought up with
.Cm net up
do not survive a reboot; render an init unit that runs it, or bring them up
from your configuration management.
.Pp
The estate view works wherever
.Xr wg 8
runs, but the container attach is Linux-only: it depends on network
namespaces.
Runtime testing to date is Linux.
